Reconstruct Play_Movie's contiguous WinMM blocks (dd2h.exe 0x414e80).
Ghidra split each argument structure into independent locals; the four-byte
local_44 passed to MCI_OPEN cannot contain its type/filename or returned ID.
The same defect affects the destination HWND, rectangle and playback callback.
Original instructions, verified with objdump:
- 414e8e passes ebp-0x40. Type is stored at -0x38 (414ea3), filename at
  -0x34 (414e8b), and returned ID loaded from -0x3c (414ec9).
- 414ebb passes ebp-0x2c; HWND is stored at -0x28 (414eb8).
- 414eef passes ebp-0x54; the rectangle DWORDs are 0 at -0x50, 48 at
  -0x4c, 640 at -0x48 and 384 at -0x44 (414ee5..414f0b).
- 414f21 passes ebp-0x1c; callback HWND is at -0x1c, and 414f2c/2f/33
  clear the following three DWORDs. Flags=1 requests the completion message.
- 414f59 passes the zero DWORD at ebp-0xc to MCI_CLOSE with WAIT=2.
Real 32-bit WinMM header offsets and native ASan/WASM API-contract fixtures
verify both success sizes, completion pumping and every early-error cleanup.
Ignored fields stay ignored, as in the original. No new commands/branches.
This restores the engine call contract; AVI decoding and actual movie A/V
remain unimplemented in the platform backend and are not claimed verified.

